    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py`. I haven't run it, since shell access wasn't available.\n\n- **`dest` handling:** an empty `dest` raises `ValueError`, and trailing `/` characters are stripped. `\"/\"` therefore becomes an empty base, so members go to `\"/name\"`.\n- **Unsafe members:** a member raises `UnsafePathError` if it contains NUL, starts with `/` or `\\`, or starts with a drive prefix such as `C:`. It also raises if a `..` would climb above the destination, or if the path is empty after normalisation.\n- **Normalisation:** backslashes are treated as separators. Empty and `.` segments are dropped, and only an exact `..` segment pops the previous one.\n- **Directory entries:** a name ending in `/` or `\\` is validated like any other member but left out of the result.\n- **Duplicates:** two file members that normalise to the same path, compared case-insensitively, raise `UnsafePathError`.\n- **Result:** every member is checked before anything is returned, so an unsafe member never yields a partial plan. The result is `dest/normalised` for each file member, in input order.",
